    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5479237/assistant-professor-of-marketing": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Current Full-Time Job Openings | Employment Opportunities For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Professor of Marketing | Employment Opportunities page has loaded. Assistant Professor of Marketing | Employment Opportunities page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Current Full-Time Job Openings Menu Current Full-Time Job Openings Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Employment Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Professor of Marketing Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Professor of Marketing Salary $100,000.00 - $106,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 27FAC676-1 Division College of Business Department Management & Marketing Opening Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement The Department of Management and Marketing at Utah Tech University in St. George, Utah, invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Marketing with a primary specialization in Product Marketing. In alignment with Utah Tech University's polytechnic mission, this tenure track faculty member will expand and enhance applied, industry-engaged learning in how organizations develop, position, differentiate, launch, manage, and grow products and brands. The position will emphasize the integration of customer insight, innovation, technology, and real-world marketing practice to prepare students for contemporary careers in product marketing and related fields. The successful candidate will contribute to the Marketing program through teaching, research, student mentoring, and engagement with industry and the broader community. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong combination of academic scholarship and professional industry experience in product marketing or closely related areas, such as product strategy, new product development, go-to-market strategy, technology commercialization, innovation, product lifecycle management, positioning, differentiation, market adoption, and customer insight. Candidates should have an active research agenda that contributes to the academic literature in product marketing or a closely related field, as well as meaningful professional experience applying these concepts in organizational settings. Professional or research experience in brand strategy and/or brand management is valued as a complement to product marketing expertise. The Utah Tech Marketing program offers a marketing BA/BS major with career-focused areas of study in Digital Marketing, Marketing Analytics, Hospitality and Services Marketing, and General Marketing, as well as a marketing minor and certificates. More information about the department, faculty, and degree offerings can be found at https://marketing.utahtech.edu/ . Responsibilities Teach and design 24 credit hours of lower- and/or upper-division courses per academic year across different delivery modalities. Courses could include Product Marketing, Marketing Strategy, Principles of Marketing, Entrepreneurial Marketing, and new upper-division electives related to product strategy, go-to-market execution, product positioning, technology marketing, innovation, or related areas. Advise undergraduate marketing students, mentor student projects, and contribute to experiential learning opportunities and industry-engaged activities. Provide institutional and campus service as defined by University Policy and the College of Business, including holding office hours, attending department and College of Business meetings and committee service in compliance with university policy. Maintain an active program of scholarly research and publication consistent with the expectations for tenure and promotion at Utah Tech University. Qualifications PhD or DBA in Marketing from an AACSB-accredited institution required; candidates who are ABD will be considered if the degree will be completed by August 2027. Active research agenda with evidence of scholarly productivity in product marketing or a closely related area, such as product management, new product development, product lifecycle management, product or marketing strategy, go-to-market strategy, positioning and differentiation, technology commercialization, innovation, market adoption or diffusion, customer insight or co-creation, portfolio strategy, emerging marketing technologies, or related areas. Demonstrated professional industry experience in product marketing, product management, go-to-market strategy and/or execution, product strategy, technology commercialization, or a closely related area is required. Demonstrated ability to design innovative, applied curriculum and deliver engaging instruction. Finalists will be required to deliver a teaching demonstration. Strong written and oral communication skills, with a proven ability to collaborate effectively within a team-oriented environment. Experience working with industry partners and incorporating experiential, project-based, or technology-enhanced learning into the classroom is preferred. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position. Faculty service with pay and benefits starting July 1, 2027. Annual salary of $100,000-$106,000 depending on qualifications and experience, with additional compensation available for optional summer/overload teaching. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, employee assistance and wellness programs, life, disability, retirement, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 12, 2026; position open until filled. Candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a one- to two-page statement describing their current and future research agenda, statement of teaching philosophy/effectiveness,contact information for three professional references (including email addresses), and transcripts. Semifinalists may be asked for a representative research paper/working paper. Please upload all the requested documents when you submit your application. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and certification of required degrees and upon successfully passing a background check. If, because of a disability, you need special services or facilities to apply for this opening, please call the Human Resources Office (435) 652-7520. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University’s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University’s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments. If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted.\r\n\r\n*Cover Letter \r\n*Curriculum Vitae\r\n*Contact information for 3 professional references (including email addresses)\r\n*Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes)\r\n*Student Success Statement\r\n\r\nHave you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold a PhD or DBA in Marketing or are you ABD with a projected completion date prior to 1 August 2027, as indicated in the job posting? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Current Full-Time Job Openings Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. Employment Opportunities Current Full-Time Job Openings Menu Close Menu Employment Opportunities Human Resources Homepage Current Full-Time Job Openings Internal Full-Time Job Postings Subscribe for Future UT F/T Job Postings Part-Time Instructor Jobs Openings Part-Time Staff Jobs Openings Right to Know Information UT Policies & Procedures Help & Support Translate SOCIAL LinkedIn Youtube Facebook Twitter Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data we collect or use, and applications owned or controlled by Governmentjobs.com, I