    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5479825/regional-admissions-counselor-for-northern-utah": {
      "title": "Position Announcement",
      "description": "Current Full-Time Job Openings | Employment Opportunities For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Regional Admissions Counselor for Northern Utah | Employment Opportunities page has loaded. Regional Admissions Counselor for Northern Utah | Employment Opportunities page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Current Full-Time Job Openings Menu Current Full-Time Job Openings Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Employment Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Regional Admissions Counselor for Northern Utah Print Apply ﻿ Regional Admissions Counselor for Northern Utah Salary $45,500.00 Annually Location Remote Worker - Northern Utah, UT Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 27PRO769-1 Division Enrollment & Marketing Department Admissions Opening Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date 9/27/2026 11:59 PM Mountain Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement Under the leadership of the Director of Admissions, the Regional Admissions Counselor is an integral part of the Admissions team by participating in recruitment of new students, including transfer students, to Utah Tech University. This position will work from home and on the road to coordinate student recruitment efforts in Northern Utah. This particular counselor will be required to live and work in Northern Utah.  Information about the Admissions department can be found online at https://admissions.utahtech.edu . Responsibilities Develop and implement a holistic recruitment strategy for prospective undergraduate students in Northern Utah and surrounding states. Building relationships with prospective students, families, school counselors, alumni, and other constituents in support of the recruitment goals. Support prospective students as they move through the recruitment process through all communication channels, answering questions about the admissions process, alleviating concerns, assisting with application submission, and following through to enrollment. This includes: Generating and analyzing enrollment analytics within the assigned territory to make data-driven recruitment decisions, identify trends, and optimize outreach strategies. Utilizing data management tools and CRM systems (Element 451) to track and assess recruitment efforts, enrollment trends, and applicant progress. Preparing reports on admissions statistics, campaign effectiveness, and recruitment ROI, offering insights and recommendations to improve enrollment strategies. Coordinate and market student recruitment events. Represent the University at college fairs, job fairs, student recruitment events, etc. Generate and analyze enrollment analytics of assigned territory and make strategic student recruitment decisions based on data analysis. Work with Ambassadors, educating them on recruiting in your prospective territory. Conduct research on student enrollment patterns and retention trends to refine outreach strategies, enhance engagement, and improve conversion rates. Collaborate with university marketing and admissions teams to develop targeted recruitment campaigns, assess their effectiveness, and refine communication strategies. Assist with any new student recruitment activities as assigned by the Director of Admissions. Leverage insights from regional research, demographic trends, and target market data to identify key recruitment opportunities, enhance marketing strategies, and tailor outreach efforts based on prospective students' needs. Measure and assess communication effectiveness within the admissions funnel, making data-driven recommendations to enhance student engagement and conversion rates. Develop predictive strategies using historical enrollment data to forecast application trends, identify high-potential prospective students, and refine marketing and recruitment strategies, ensuring targeted and efficient outreach efforts. Conduct A/B testing on individual email outreach to optimize engagement, improve response rates, and tailor messaging based on student behavior and performance data. Perform other duties as assigned. This position will require local travel in support of student recruitment activities. Local travel will be required for extended periods of time. Position will be required to live in Northern Utah (Davis County, Salt Lake County, or Utah County) and perform administrative tasks from a home office when not traveling for recruitment events and activities. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in a related field required; a combination of relevant education and experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis. Ability to live in the assigned regional area and work from home required. Ability to travel in support of student recruitment activities, both for short and extended periods of time. Experience in relationship building, marketing, or sales preferred; experience in student recruitment and student leadership preferred. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work under pressure and professionally handle multiple/competing priorities. Ability to exercise critical thinking skills to improve workload. Comfortable in a university environment working with students, faculty, and staff from multiple backgrounds and nationalities. Ability to work effectively in a team environment. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time overtime-exempt staff position. Annual salary of $45,500 with a desired start date of November 2026. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, as well as paid holidays in addition to sick and vacation leave accruals. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins September 28, 2026 . Submit application materials (including resume contents and contact information for three professional references) and upload a cover letter electronically. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University’s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University’s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments.  If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted.\r\n\r\nCover Letter \r\nResume \r\nContact information (including email) for three professional references\r\n\r\nHave you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold at least a Bachelor's degree in the required area for this position by the desired start date? A combination of relevant education and experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis. Yes No 03 Do you currently have the ability to live in the assigned regional area, to work from home, and to travel in support of student recruitment activities, both for short and extended periods of time? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Current Full-Time Job Openings Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. Employment Opportunities Current Full-Time Job Openings Menu Close Menu Employment Opportunities Human Resources Homepage Current Full-Time Job Openings Internal Full-Time Job Postings Subscribe for Future UT F/T Job Postings Part-Time Instructor Jobs Openings Part-Time Staff Jobs Openings Right to Know Information UT Policies & Procedures Help & Support Translate SOCIAL LinkedIn Youtube Facebook Twitter Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data we collect or use, and applications owned or controlled by Governmentjobs.com, Inc. (DBA “NEOGOV”), including our related brands NEOGOV.com, NEOED.com, PowerDMS.com, Governmentjobs.com,