    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/utahtech/jobs/5490984/assistant-director-higher-education-for-incarcerated-youth-heiy": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Higher Education for Incarcerated Youth (HEIY)",
      "description": "Current Full-Time Job Openings | Employment Opportunities For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Director, Higher Education for Incarcerated Youth (HEIY) | Employment Opportunities page has loaded. Assistant Director, Higher Education for Incarcerated Youth (HEIY) | Employment Opportunities page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Current Full-Time Job Openings Menu Current Full-Time Job Openings Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Employment Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Director, Higher Education for Incarcerated Youth (HEIY) Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Director, Higher Education for Incarcerated Youth (HEIY) Salary $54,000.00 - $57,000.00 Annually Location Main Campus - 225 S University Ave, St. George 84770, UT Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 27PRO633-1 Division Academic Affairs Department Academic Community Engagement Opening Date 09/22/2026 Closing Date 10/11/2026 11:59 PM Mountain Description Benefits Questions Position Announcement Utah Tech University seeks a detail-oriented, highly collaborative, and collegial Assistant Director for Higher Education for Incarcerated Youth (HEIY). This position serves as a key internal operations leader and liaison between Utah Tech University and partnering juvenile justice facilities, supporting the implementation and day-to-day coordination of postsecondary educational programming for justice-involved youth across Utah. Working under the guidance of the HEIY Director and the Executive Director for Early College Outreach, the Assistant Director manages and implements program operations, instructional coordination, student support systems, and student data tracking across multiple sites. The position helps establish and maintain consistent procedures, supports instructional staff, and expands incarcerated youth access to high-quality academics, university resources, and educational opportunities. Because HEIY students may have limited or no direct access to university portals, email, Canvas, or other electronic communication, the Assistant Director serves as an essential academic bridge, information-processing specialist, and operational proxy helping students, faculty, facility personnel, and university offices exchange the information and materials necessary to maintain academic continuity. The Assistant Director will manage virtual and asynchronous instruction across the program. They may also teach courses as assigned by the Director and academic leadership. Position funded through June 30, 2028, dependent upon funding thereafter. Responsibilities Program Operations and Coordination Support implementation of HEIY programming across participating juvenile justice facilities through communication, coordination, and alignment with university policies, facility requirements, and applicable regulations. Develop, document, and maintain standardized procedures for enrollment, course delivery, student tracking, scheduling, and multi-site program logistics. Coordinate instructional logistics across sites and help ensure consistent, accurate, and compliant program operations. Maintain accurate student tracking systems to account for student enrollment, academic progress, course participation, and movement among participating facilities. Respond flexibly and positively to student transfers, releases, facility scheduling changes, and other changing circumstances that may affect academic continuity. Synthesize information received from multiple partners, including facility personnel, school district representatives, educators, and university offices into accurate and usable program and student records. Maintain exceptional accuracy and attention to detail in program documentation, enrollment information, academic records, and operational data. Instruction and Academic Support Facilitate online and asynchronous coursework for HEIY students, ensuring access, engagement, and academic progress. Support faculty and instructional staff through coordination of course materials, classroom logistics, assignments, and access to Canvas and other learning resources. Serve as an academic intermediary between university faculty and HEIY students who may not have direct access to university communication systems or academic portals. Facilitate the timely delivery of physical and digital course materials to participating facilities and assist with the secure return and submission of completed student work to instructors’ LMS (Canvas) pages. Work creatively and collaboratively with faculty and facility personnel to address barriers to student participation and academic progress. Technology-Enhanced Instruction and Communication Coordinate, host, and facilitate live virtual instruction in partnership with faculty and juvenile justice facility staff. Provide a welcoming, patient, respectful, and supportive presence during virtual instruction, technology troubleshooting, and interactions with students and staff. Serve as liaison between faculty, students, and facilities, ensuring clear communication of expectations, schedules, course needs, and instructional changes. Troubleshoot instructional technologies and user-interface issues within university-supported systems, including Zoom, Canvas, and secure learning environments. Assist faculty and students with technology-related instructional logistics when direct student access to university systems is limited. Student Progression, Administrative, & Other Responsibilities Collaborate with the Director to enhance student support services, retention, reentry pathways, and efforts to address barriers to student engagement and success. Assist with recruitment, hiring, onboarding, training, and supervision of instructional staff and HEIY program assistants. Assist with planning and coordinating program events, including graduations at juvenile justice facilities. Track student progress by course towards the General Education certificate, associate degree, and bachelor’s degree. Apply for graduation on behalf of students, obtain LMS access for students, and coordinate future course and graduation pathways for HEIY participants. Ensure consistency in instructional expectations and program delivery and provide ongoing support to instructors working in correctional education settings. Assist the Director in aligning program operations, Under the advisement of the Director, align program operations, track data and student outcomes, maintain records, support reporting, and contribute to continuous program improvement and program sustainability. Maintain accurate program data related to enrollment, course completion, academic progress, certificates and degrees, and other identified outcomes. Assist in preparing accurate program reports and summaries for university leadership, partner organizations, and other authorized stakeholders. Preserve and protect confidential student and partner information, including academic records, student locations, educational needs, and other protected information obtained through program operations. Map student graduation pathways, apply for graduation on behalf of qualified students, obtain necessary LMS access, and coordinate future course pathways for HEIY participants Perform other duties as assigned in support of the HEIY program and Utah Tech University's educational mission. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in any subject, required. Master’s degree preferred. Training or experience developing and maintaining databases and tracking systems using Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, or comparable software. Demonstrated ability in information and data processing and creating accurate and aesthetic illustrations of data. Demonstrated ability to coordinate and collaborate effectively with educational institutions, government facilities, community partners, and cross-agency stakeholders. Strong organizational and operational skills, including developing procedures, documentation, tracking systems, and workflows, with exceptional attention to detail and the ability to coordinate complex initiatives. Demonstrated ability to organize, verify, maintain, and synthesize information or data obtained from multiple sources of information from government agencies and partners. Strong technology skills and demonstrated ability to learn and effectively use systems necessary for virtual instruction, academic coordination, data management, and communication. Demonstrated professionalism, discretion, sound judgment, and ability to maintain confidentiality when working with sensitive or protected information. Supplemental Information POSITION DETAILS, COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS: Full-time overtime-exempt staff position. Annual salary of $54,000-$57,000 depending on qualifications and experience. Position funded through June 30, 2028, dependent upon funding thereafter. Desired start date of November/December 2026. Excellent benefits package included that begins on start date; includes medical, dental, vision, disability, and life insurance, employee assistance and wellness programs, retirement plan contributions, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and eligible dependents, as well as paid holidays in addition to sick and vacation leave accruals. See https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ under \"Benefits Summary\" for more details. ELECTRONIC APPLICATION PROCEDURES: Application review begins October 12, 2026 . Submit application materials (including resume contents and contact information for three professional references) and upload a cover letter electronically. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: Utah Tech University is an open, comprehensive, polytechnic institution, committed to exceptional student learning and success that has adopted an instructional approach of \"active learning. active life.\" and a culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered. Established in 1911 as a community college and in 2013 as a state university, our University is located in picturesque southwestern Utah, approximately 120 miles northeast of Las Vegas. The area is renowned for its red rocks, desert climate, over 300 days of sunshine annually, and featuring easy access to world-class outdoor recreational opportunities. Click here to learn more about the University . Utah Tech University is a fast-growing Utah public institution of higher education, with more than 13,000 students. We offer over 250 programs, including doctoral, masters, bachelors, associates, certificates, endorsements, minors, and/or emphases. We seek faculty and staff committed to creating an active, applied, and career-oriented learning environment that is student-centered, who bring new ideas, possess values and career aspirations aligned with the University’s mission and vision, and are inspired to build a premier open, comprehensive, polytechnic university. Utah Tech employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must provide employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. Utah Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, please contact Human Resources at hr@utahtech.edu or 435-652-7500. Utah Tech University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, citizenship, sex (including sex discrimination and sexual harassment), sexual orientation, gender identity, age, ancestry, disability status, pregnancy, pregnancy-related conditions, genetic information, military status, veteran status, or other bases protected by applicable law in employment, treatment, admission, access to educational programs and activities, or other University benefits or services. For more information or contact information, please visit https://titleix.utahtech.edu/reporting-discrimination/ . For important information regarding academics, campus safety, student services, employment laws, and other regulatory requirements, visit Utah Tech University’s Right-to-Know https://utahtech.edu/right-to-know/ and Clery Act https://police.utahtech.edu/clery-act websites. Click here to visit https://humanresources.utahtech.edu/employee-benefits/ to learn more about the wonderful benefits available to you as a Utah Tech employee! Highlights from Utah Tech's benefits package include: 14.2% retirement contribution, paid 100% by the employer (no match required), vested on day 1 of full-time employment; Regular undergraduate tuition waiver (paid at 100%) for employee, spouse, and unmarried dependent children to take courses at Utah Tech; Full medical, dental, and vision plans, with low employee-paid premiums, that begins on day 1 of full-time employment; Flexible Spending Accounts or Health Savings Accounts available; Employer-paid basic life insurance & disability insurance coverage from day 1 of full-time employment; Generous staff leave accruals, plus 12 paid holidays per calendar year. 01 The following attachments are required to apply for this position. The size limit on a single attachment is 5 MB. You may attach up to 10 attachments.  If you do not submit all of the required documents, your application may not receive full consideration. You will not be able to edit or add to your application once it has been submitted.\r\n\r\nCover Letter \r\nResume \r\nContact information (including email) for three professional references\r\n\r\nHave you uploaded these documents? Yes No 02 Will you hold at least a Bachelor's degree in the required area for this position by the desired start date? Yes No Required Question Employer Utah Tech University Address Human Resources 225 S. University Avenue St. George, Utah, 84770 Phone 435-652-4520 Website http://humanresources.utahtech.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Current Full-Time Job Openings Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. Employment Opportunities Current Full-Time Job Openings Menu Close Menu Employment Opportunities Human Resources Homepage Current Full-Time Job Openings Internal Full-Time Job Postings Subscribe for Future UT F/T Job Postings Part-Time Instructor Jobs Openings Part-Time Staff Jobs Openings Right to Know Information UT Policies & Procedures Help & Support Translate SOCIAL LinkedIn Youtube Facebook Twitter Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data we collect or use, and applications owned or controlled by Governmentjobs.com, Inc. (DBA “NEOGOV”), including our related brands NEOGOV.com, NEOED.com, PowerDMS.com, Governmentjobs.com, Schooljobs.com, and our mobile app(s) (collectively referred to as the “Services”), or affiliated companies (collectively referred to herein as “Governmentjobs”, \"Schooljobs\", “NEOGOV”, “NEOED”, “PowerDMS”, “we”, “us”, or “our”). By using any part of the Services you agree that you have read this Policy, your personal data will be processed as described herein, and you agree to be bound by this Policy. This Policy is incorporated into our Terms of Use . Definitions not explicitly defined herein shall retain the meaning as prescribed in the Terms of Use . Any dispute related to privacy is subject to the Terms of Use and this Policy, including limitations on liability. This Policy does not apply to (1) personal data controlled by our Customers (employers that utilize our Services, described further below), which is governed by our separate agreements and related data processing agreements with such Customers; (2) personal data collected by unaffilia"
